      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "Scanning Electron Micrograph (SEM) of <i>Trypanosoma brucei brucei</i> in the liver of an infected mouse, surrounded by host immune cells. The image shows the elongated trypanosome navigating through hepatic tissue, with nearby leukocytes interacting with the parasite\n<p>Colors are artificially added to enhance contrast between the parasite (blue) and host cells (beige).\n</p>\n<ul><li>Instrument: FEI Quanta FEG (CMMI, Gosselies)</li>\n<li>Detector: Everhart–Thornley Detector (ETD)</li>\n<li>Accelerating voltage: 30 kV</li>\n<li>Working distance: 9.3 mm</li>\n<li>Magnification: 30,000×</li>\n<li>Horizontal field width: 9.01 µm</li>\n<li>Scan time: 35.22 s (single-frame acquisition)</li></ul>\nScale bar removed during cropping; dimensions based on instrument calibration. Image created by Bérénice Veraghen.",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
      },
